# Zentra - Dev Guard

## Phase 1: Select the change

Default to the union of staged, unstaged and untracked nonignored files using `git diff --name-status`, `git diff --cached --name-status` and `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`. Include deletions, renames, HTML/CSS, manifests, lockfiles, scripts and CI/configuration. For an explicit commit range use that range; for a path use the given scope. Exclude vendor/generated output with reasons. If scope is empty, say so without issuing a security pass.

Read the diff and relevant surrounding functions/callers to establish effective controls. Do not broaden to a full-repository assessment. Do not write `.zentra/`, create hooks, install tools, run application scripts or spawn subagents in this lightweight mode.

## Phase 2: Check affected invariants

Check secrets (redacted locations only), injection paths, object/action/tenant permissions, token/session validation, data exposure, file/URL/process boundaries, resource limits, error paths, transaction/race invariants and AI/tool output trust. Include dependency resolution and delivery changes; unavailable advisory data is a disclosed gap.

For web changes consult modern-web-guidance when available or primary MDN/W3C/web.dev guidance. Check context-specific escaping, sanitizer configuration, CSRF/cookies/CORS, keyboard/focus/labels, supported fallbacks and obvious performance regressions. Read global middleware before flagging missing local auth. Public routes, fixtures, visual randomness, checksums and GraphQL introspection are not automatically vulnerabilities.

## Phase 3: Inline report

For each candidate give impact-based severity, `file:line`, attacker input -> boundary -> effect, examined defenses, uncertainty and correction. Distinguish candidates from verified findings and security defects from accessibility/performance hardening. Never print secret values. Summarize coverage and checks not executed. If none are found, say "No candidates found in the reviewed change; independent/runtime verification was not performed."

For strict acceptance suggest zentra-verify; this quick review cannot issue its pass. If asked for commit hooks, inspect the actual agent/version hook API and use deterministic exit codes rather than parsing an LLM's PASS/BLOCK prose. Do not invent configuration keys or install hooks without authorization.
